# Alternate start codes (ANSI E1.11): anything but 0x00. The slots are not
# levels, so the meaning gives them as data. Known codes are named; any other
# is kept as `alternate 0xNN` and re-encoded as it came.

# An RDM start code (ANSI E1.20, 0xCC) with the sub-start-code 0x01 and a
# message's first octets: carried here as opaque data until Phase 6b.
cc 01 18 7a 70 => rdm 4 slots; data 01187a70
# ASCII text, 0x17: "FOH".
17 46 4f 48 => text 3 slots; data 464f48
# A System Information Packet, 0xCF, alone.
cf => sip 0 slots; no data
# Start codes this crate does not name round-trip untouched.
55 55 aa => alternate 0x55 2 slots; data 55aa
91 7a 70 01 => alternate 0x91 3 slots; data 7a7001
# 0xFF is a start code like any other.
ff 00 => alternate 0xff 1 slots; data 00
